FUNCTION_BLOCK "FB_ScanLineJob"
{ S7_Optimized_Access := 'TRUE' }
VERSION : 0.2
// 2026-11-09. one button, one line scan: n straight lines at one height. with the two switches it
// is a serpentine (zigzag), a raster (one way) or a patch scan (index along the line). same shape
// as fb_scancubejob and fb_scandrumjob: build the geometry, check it, push, count. no motion
// code, the engine does the rest. runs in ob1 after the drum job, instance "IDB_ScanLineJob",
// job 3 in fc_jobmux. spec and the reasons: check_other_ideas_changes_critiqe/SCAN_TYPES.md
// sections 4, 5, 7 (decided 2026-11-08, the build released 2026-11-09 after the drum ran).
//
// v0.1 (2026-11-09): the job as described below, the list of moves kept in arrays of 203 entries,
// at most 50 lines (job error 5 above that).
// v0.2 (2026-11-09, the same day, the whole table): two things.
//    1. no list any more. the geometry is frozen into udtGeo ("UDT_LineGeo") at the start and every
//       move is computed from its index by "FC_LineMove" when it is pushed. the moves, their order,
//       their ids and the line numbers are exactly those of v0.1. the limit of 50 lines is gone:
//       up to MAX_LINES = 5000 lines (the move counters are int). the check before the first push
//       covers the whole job without a list: every point of the job lies inside the parallelogram
//       of the four outer line ends, at the scan height, at safe z and at lift z, with both rotz
//       values; those corners go through fc_posecheck (24 poses at most), plus pose 2 and pose 1.
//       the engine checks every target again in its step 5, as always.
//    2. AREA mode, i_xArea = "DB_Recipe".Line.xArea, off = exactly v0.1. on = the area is given
//       by two corners instead of length and lines: pose 9 is corner 1 (as before, the start of
//       line 0), pose 10 is the opposite corner 2. the angle sets the axis of the lines; the job
//       takes the extent of corner 2 along that axis as the length and the extent across it,
//       divided by the pitch, as the number of lines (plus one), and the side from where corner 2
//       lies, so the sign of the pitch does not matter. if corner 2 lies behind corner 1 along the
//       axis, the axis is turned by 180, so the lines always run from corner 1 toward corner 2.
//       with INDEX ALONG the length stays the typed patch length and the patches are set along the
//       axis up to corner 2, pitch apart. the lines field is ignored, o_intLineCount shows what was
//       computed. the last line lies at most one pitch before corner 2 (floor). pose 10 not taught
//       = job error 1; corner 2 on the across line only (length 0) or more than MAX_LINES lines =
//       job error 5. scan from here works with it: the actual pose is corner 1, pose 10 corner 2.
//    long lines at a low override take longer than the engine's 60 s: fb_robotmove v0.8 adds the
//    distance divided by "DB_RobotMove".Cfg.rMinSpeed to the time limit (0 = as before).
//
// program 20: block 1 (linear) for every index, lift and travel move, block 2 (linear slow) for
// the scan lines and for the moves down onto a line. nothing new in program 20,
// Cfg.intBlocksInPrg20 stays 4.
//
// what it needs (hmi: the LINE box, hmi_stage2.md section 7):
//    pose 9      the start of line 0: jog the tool to the first point that is to be scanned, at
//                any height, TEACH 9. x, y, rotz and roty of it are used, the height is Line.rZ.
//                with i_xFromHere the actual pose is the start instead, nothing is stored
//    pose 10     area mode only: the opposite corner of the area, any height, TEACH 10. x, y used
//    pose 2      start, pose 1 home (optional), rSafeZ, as for the cube and the drum
//    Line.rLength      mm, the patch: the part of every line that is scanned. 0 = job error 5.
//                      area mode without index along: not used, the length comes from corner 2
//    Line.rPitch       mm, start to start between two lines. the sign is the side: + = the next
//                      line lies to the left of the line direction (+90 deg), - = to the right.
//                      0 = job error 5. area mode: only the size counts, the side comes from corner 2
//    Line.intCount     lines, 1 .. MAX_LINES (5000). area mode: not used, computed
//    Line.rLeadIn      mm, every line begins this much before its patch and ends this much after
//                      it, so the ramps lie outside the patch (SCAN_TYPES.md 3.2). 0 allowed
//    Line.rAngle       deg, direction of the lines in the base system, 0 = +x, 90 = +y
//    Line.rZ           mm, scan height
//    Line.rFaceZ       mm, the face that is scanned. 0 = not checked. smaller z is up on this
//                      machine (seen 2026-11-05 and 11-06): rZ must be smaller than it, else
//                      job error 9
//    Line.rRotZOffset  deg, the tool rotz when it looks along +x, as Drum.rRotZOffset
//    Line.xZigzag      off = raster: every line runs in the same direction, the index move is the
//                      long diagonal back. on = serpentine: every odd line runs backwards
//    Line.xIndexAlong  off = the next line lies beside this one (raster, serpentine). on = the
//                      next line lies further along the same line (the patch scan, pitch > length)
//    Line.xLiftBetween off = the index move runs at the scan height. on = lift, travel, down
//                      between two lines (the retract of the patch scan)
//    Line.rLiftZ       mm, the height of the travel with lift between. 0 = rSafeZ
//    Line.xArea        v0.2: the area by two corners, pose 9 and pose 10, see above
//    xNoTurn           "DB_Recipe".xNoTurn, the switch of the cube and the drum. on = every point
//                      keeps the rotz of pose 9 (the proven way, the first run). off = the tool
//                      looks along the line, rotz = rAngle + rRotZOffset; in the serpentine it is
//                      turned 180 on every odd line, inside the index move (SCAN_TYPES.md 7.5)
//
// the moves. intId = the kind of move (hmi text TL_MoveLine), o_intLineActive = the line k:
//     1 to start (pose 2)            2 above line 0 at safe z         3 down onto line 0, slow
//     4 scan line k, slow            5 index to line k+1             6 lift between (to lift z)
//     7 travel at lift z             8 down onto line k+1, slow      9 lift to safe z
//    10 to start (pose 2)           11 home (pose 1), only if pose 1 is taught
// moves total = 3 + n + (n - 1) * 1 (or * 3 with lift between) + 2, + 1 with home, - 1 with
// scan from here (no "to start" at the beginning). the order, move by move: fc_linemove.
//
// geometry. d = (cos a, sin a) the line direction, e = (-sin a, cos a) across it, to the left.
//    a_k = a_0 + k * pitch * e   (index across)       a_k = a_0 + k * pitch * d   (index along)
//    the line k runs from a_k - leadin * d to a_k + (length + leadin) * d; an odd line of the
//    serpentine runs the same two points the other way round. the patch k is a_k .. a_k + length * d,
//    the window bit o_xScanWindow is on while the actual x y lie inside it during the line move.
//
// the queue holds 50 entries: this block pushes while the queue has fewer than QUEUE_KEEP entries,
// one per cycle, not everything at once as the drum job does.
   VAR_INPUT
      i_xStart : Bool;                          // hmi button, momentary, gated by Man.intJob = 3 in ob1
      i_xAbort : Bool;                          // hmi button, momentary. also clears a job error
      i_xAuto : Bool;                           // auto switch and enable. falls while running = abort
      i_intOverride : Int;                      // % for every move
      i_aoudtP : Array[1..50] of "UDT_Pose";    // "DB_Poses".aoudtP
      i_aoxValid : Array[1..50] of Bool;        // "DB_Poses".aoxValid
      i_rSafeZ : Real;                          // "DB_Poses".rSafeZ
      i_rLength : Real;                         // "DB_Recipe".Line.rLength
      i_rPitch : Real;                          // "DB_Recipe".Line.rPitch
      i_intCount : Int;                         // "DB_Recipe".Line.intCount
      i_rLeadIn : Real;                         // "DB_Recipe".Line.rLeadIn
      i_rAngle : Real;                          // "DB_Recipe".Line.rAngle
      i_rZ : Real;                              // "DB_Recipe".Line.rZ
      i_rFaceZ : Real;                          // "DB_Recipe".Line.rFaceZ
      i_rRotZOffset : Real;                     // "DB_Recipe".Line.rRotZOffset
      i_xZigzag : Bool;                         // "DB_Recipe".Line.xZigzag
      i_xIndexAlong : Bool;                     // "DB_Recipe".Line.xIndexAlong
      i_xLiftBetween : Bool;                    // "DB_Recipe".Line.xLiftBetween
      i_rLiftZ : Real;                          // "DB_Recipe".Line.rLiftZ
      i_udtMoveState : "UDT_MoveState";         // "DB_RobotMove".State
      i_intQueueCount : Int;                    // "DB_MoveQueue".intCount
      i_xFromHere : Bool;                       // "DB_Recipe".xFromHere: the actual pose is the start of line 0
      i_udtActual : "UDT_Pose";                 // "DB_Robot".Status.udtPoseBcs. also read for the window bit
      i_xActualValid : Bool;                    // "DB_Robot".Status.xReferenced AND .xCommOK
      i_xNoTurn : Bool;                         // "DB_Recipe".xNoTurn: every point keeps the rotz of pose 9
      i_xArea : Bool;                           // v0.2: "DB_Recipe".Line.xArea, the area by pose 9 and pose 10. off = v0.1
   END_VAR

   VAR_OUTPUT
      o_udtOut : "UDT_JobOut";                  // => "DB_RobotJob".Line
      o_xScanWindow : Bool;                     // => "DB_RobotJob".xScanWindow. on while the tool is inside a patch during a line move
      o_intLineActive : Int;                    // => "DB_RobotJob".intLineActive. the line k (0 .. n-1) of the active move
      o_intLineCount : Int;                     // v0.2: => "DB_RobotJob".intLineCount. the lines of the job as built (typed, or computed in area mode)
   END_VAR

   VAR
      intStep : Int;                            // 0 idle, 10 build, 20 push while the queue has room, 30 run out, 90 error
      xStartOld : Bool;
      xAbortOld : Bool;
      udtGeo : "UDT_LineGeo";                   // v0.2: the frozen geometry of the running job. fc_linemove computes every move from it
      intPushIdx : Int;                         // the next move to push, 1 .. udtGeo.intMoves
   END_VAR

   VAR_TEMP
      tmp_xStartEdge : Bool;
      tmp_xAbortEdge : Bool;
      tmp_intErr : Int;
      tmp_intPoseErr : Int;
      tmp_intActive : Int;
      tmp_intFirst : Int;
      tmp_intCount : Int;
      tmp_intC : Int;
      tmp_intH : Int;
      tmp_intRot : Int;
      tmp_intK : Int;
      tmp_intKind : Int;
      tmp_rRad : Real;
      tmp_rAngle : Real;
      tmp_rDirX : Real;
      tmp_rDirY : Real;
      tmp_rVX : Real;
      tmp_rVY : Real;
      tmp_rAlong : Real;
      tmp_rAcross : Real;
      tmp_rLength : Real;
      tmp_rPitch : Real;
      tmp_rPitchAbs : Real;
      tmp_rRotZEven : Real;
      tmp_rRotZOdd : Real;
      tmp_rAX : Real;
      tmp_rAY : Real;
      tmp_rP : Real;
      tmp_udtA0 : "UDT_Pose";
      tmp_udtP : "UDT_Pose";
   END_VAR

   VAR CONSTANT
      P_HOME : Int := 1;
      P_START : Int := 2;
      P_LINE : Int := 9;                        // the start of line 0, db_poses row 9 (corner 1 in area mode)
      P_CORNER2 : Int := 10;                    // v0.2: the opposite corner of the area, db_poses row 10. area mode only
      BLOCK_LIN : Int := 1;                     // program 20 block 1, linear normal
      BLOCK_LIN_SLOW : Int := 2;                // block 2, linear slow: the scan lines and the moves down onto a line
      ID_START : Int := 1;
      ID_ABOVE : Int := 2;
      ID_DOWN0 : Int := 3;
      ID_LINE : Int := 4;
      ID_INDEX : Int := 5;
      ID_LIFT : Int := 6;
      ID_TRAVEL : Int := 7;
      ID_DOWN : Int := 8;
      ID_LIFT_END : Int := 9;
      ID_START2 : Int := 10;
      ID_HOME : Int := 11;
      MAX_LINES : Int := 5000;                  // v0.2: 50 in v0.1. the move counters are int: 4 * 5000 + 5 fits
      QUEUE_KEEP : Int := 8;                    // push while the queue holds fewer than this. the queue takes 50
      DEG_TO_RAD : Real := 0.017453293;         // pi / 180
      AREA_EPS : Real := 0.01;                  // mm, so that an extent of exactly n pitches gives n + 1 lines
   END_VAR

BEGIN
   // ---- edges and pulses -------------------------------------------------------
   #tmp_xStartEdge := #i_xStart AND NOT #xStartOld;
   #xStartOld := #i_xStart;
   #tmp_xAbortEdge := #i_xAbort AND NOT #xAbortOld;
   #xAbortOld := #i_xAbort;

   #o_udtOut.xPushReq := FALSE;
   #o_udtOut.xClear := FALSE;
   #o_udtOut.udtState.xDone := FALSE;

   // ---- abort while running: button, auto off, or the engine went into error ---------
   IF #intStep >= 10 AND #intStep <= 30 THEN
      IF #tmp_xAbortEdge OR NOT #i_xAuto THEN
         #o_udtOut.xClear := TRUE;              // the running move finishes, nothing follows
         #o_udtOut.udtState.xRunning := FALSE;
         #intStep := 0;
      ELSIF #i_udtMoveState.xError THEN
         #o_udtOut.xClear := TRUE;
         #o_udtOut.udtState.intErrId := 10;
         #o_udtOut.udtState.intEngineErr := #i_udtMoveState.intErrId;
         #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := #i_udtMoveState.intIdActive;
         #intStep := 90;
      END_IF;
   END_IF;

   CASE #intStep OF
      0: // idle
         #o_udtOut.udtState.xRunning := FALSE;
         IF #tmp_xStartEdge AND #i_xAuto THEN
            #o_udtOut.udtState.xError := FALSE;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intErrId := 0;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intEngineErr := 0;
            #o_intLineActive := 0;
            #intStep := 10;
         END_IF;

      10: // build the geometry and check it. nothing goes out of this block yet
         #tmp_intErr := 0;
         IF NOT #i_aoxValid[#P_START] OR (NOT #i_aoxValid[#P_LINE] AND NOT #i_xFromHere)
            OR (#i_xArea AND NOT #i_aoxValid[#P_CORNER2]) THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 1;                   // start, the line start, or corner 2 of the area not taught
         END_IF;
         IF #i_xFromHere AND NOT #i_xActualValid THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 6;                   // scan from here: the actual pose is not valid
         END_IF;
         IF #i_rSafeZ <= 0.0 THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 2;                   // safe z not set
         END_IF;
         IF #i_udtMoveState.xBusy OR #i_udtMoveState.xError THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 3;                   // engine busy or in error
         END_IF;
         IF #i_rPitch = 0.0 OR #i_rLeadIn < 0.0 THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 5;                   // pitch 0 or a negative lead-in
         END_IF;
         IF NOT #i_xArea AND (#i_rLength <= 0.0 OR #i_intCount < 1 OR #i_intCount > #MAX_LINES) THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 5;                   // length 0 or the lines outside 1 .. MAX_LINES (typed mode)
         END_IF;
         IF #i_xArea AND #i_xIndexAlong AND #i_rLength <= 0.0 THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 5;                   // area mode with index along: the patch length is still typed
         END_IF;
         IF #i_rFaceZ <> 0.0 AND #i_rZ >= #i_rFaceZ THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 9;                   // the scan height is not above the face (smaller z is up)
         END_IF;

         IF #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
            // the start of line 0: the actual pose with "scan from here", else pose 9. the height is the scan height
            IF #i_xFromHere THEN
               #tmp_udtA0 := #i_udtActual;
               #tmp_intFirst := 2;              // the robot stands at the start: no "to start" first
            ELSE
               #tmp_udtA0 := #i_aoudtP[#P_LINE];
               #tmp_intFirst := 1;
            END_IF;
            #tmp_udtA0.rZ := #i_rZ;

            // the line direction d from the angle
            #tmp_rAngle := #i_rAngle;
            #tmp_rRad := #tmp_rAngle * #DEG_TO_RAD;
            #tmp_rDirX := COS(#tmp_rRad);
            #tmp_rDirY := SIN(#tmp_rRad);

            IF #i_xArea THEN
               // v0.2: the area by its two corners. corner 2 relative to corner 1, split along d and across it (to the left)
               #tmp_rVX := #i_aoudtP[#P_CORNER2].rX - #tmp_udtA0.rX;
               #tmp_rVY := #i_aoudtP[#P_CORNER2].rY - #tmp_udtA0.rY;
               #tmp_rAlong := #tmp_rVX * #tmp_rDirX + #tmp_rVY * #tmp_rDirY;
               #tmp_rAcross := -#tmp_rVX * #tmp_rDirY + #tmp_rVY * #tmp_rDirX;
               IF #tmp_rAlong < 0.0 THEN
                  // corner 2 lies behind corner 1 along the axis: turn the axis by 180, the lines then run toward corner 2
                  #tmp_rAngle := #tmp_rAngle + 180.0;
                  IF #tmp_rAngle > 180.0 THEN
                     #tmp_rAngle := #tmp_rAngle - 360.0;
                  END_IF;
                  #tmp_rDirX := -#tmp_rDirX;
                  #tmp_rDirY := -#tmp_rDirY;
                  #tmp_rAlong := -#tmp_rAlong;
                  #tmp_rAcross := -#tmp_rAcross;
               END_IF;
               #tmp_rPitchAbs := ABS(#i_rPitch);
               IF #i_xIndexAlong THEN
                  // the patches lie along the axis from corner 1 up to corner 2, pitch apart. the patch length stays typed
                  #tmp_rLength := #i_rLength;
                  #tmp_rPitch := #tmp_rPitchAbs;
                  // floor(along / pitch) + 1. real_to_int rounds, so half a step is taken off first
                  #tmp_intCount := REAL_TO_INT((#tmp_rAlong + #AREA_EPS) / #tmp_rPitchAbs - 0.5) + 1;
               ELSE
                  // the lines run from corner 1 toward corner 2 along the axis; the rows walk across to corner 2
                  #tmp_rLength := #tmp_rAlong;
                  IF #tmp_rAcross >= 0.0 THEN
                     #tmp_rPitch := #tmp_rPitchAbs;        // corner 2 lies to the left: the rows walk left
                  ELSE
                     #tmp_rPitch := -#tmp_rPitchAbs;       // to the right
                  END_IF;
                  #tmp_intCount := REAL_TO_INT((ABS(#tmp_rAcross) + #AREA_EPS) / #tmp_rPitchAbs - 0.5) + 1;
               END_IF;
               IF #tmp_rLength <= 0.0 OR #tmp_intCount < 1 THEN
                  #tmp_intErr := 5;             // corner 2 lies on the across line of corner 1: no length along the axis
               ELSIF #tmp_intCount > #MAX_LINES THEN
                  #tmp_intErr := 5;             // more than MAX_LINES lines: a larger pitch
               END_IF;
            ELSE
               #tmp_rLength := #i_rLength;
               #tmp_rPitch := #i_rPitch;
               #tmp_intCount := #i_intCount;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;

         IF #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
            // the rotz of the even and the odd lines (SCAN_TYPES.md 7.5). no turn: the rotz of the start everywhere.
            // else the tool looks along the line, and the odd line of the serpentine is turned 180 the way that
            // stays inside -180 .. +180
            IF #i_xNoTurn THEN
               #tmp_rRotZEven := #tmp_udtA0.rRotZ;
               #tmp_rRotZOdd := #tmp_udtA0.rRotZ;
            ELSE
               #tmp_rRotZEven := #tmp_rAngle + #i_rRotZOffset;
               IF #tmp_rRotZEven > 180.0 THEN
                  #tmp_rRotZEven := #tmp_rRotZEven - 360.0;
               ELSIF #tmp_rRotZEven < -180.0 THEN
                  #tmp_rRotZEven := #tmp_rRotZEven + 360.0;
               END_IF;
               IF #i_xZigzag THEN
                  IF #tmp_rRotZEven <= 0.0 THEN
                     #tmp_rRotZOdd := #tmp_rRotZEven + 180.0;
                  ELSE
                     #tmp_rRotZOdd := #tmp_rRotZEven - 180.0;
                  END_IF;
               ELSE
                  #tmp_rRotZOdd := #tmp_rRotZEven;
               END_IF;
            END_IF;

            // ---- freeze the geometry. from here on fc_linemove gives every move of the job ----
            #udtGeo.intCount := #tmp_intCount;
            #udtGeo.intFirst := #tmp_intFirst;
            #udtGeo.xHome := #i_aoxValid[#P_HOME];
            #udtGeo.xLift := #i_xLiftBetween;
            #udtGeo.xZigzag := #i_xZigzag;
            #udtGeo.rA0X := #tmp_udtA0.rX;
            #udtGeo.rA0Y := #tmp_udtA0.rY;
            #udtGeo.rRotY := #tmp_udtA0.rRotY;
            #udtGeo.rDirX := #tmp_rDirX;
            #udtGeo.rDirY := #tmp_rDirY;
            IF #i_xIndexAlong THEN
               #udtGeo.rIdxX := #tmp_rDirX;     // the next line further along the same line
               #udtGeo.rIdxY := #tmp_rDirY;
            ELSE
               #udtGeo.rIdxX := -#tmp_rDirY;    // e, across the lines, to the left of d
               #udtGeo.rIdxY := #tmp_rDirX;
            END_IF;
            #udtGeo.rPitch := #tmp_rPitch;
            #udtGeo.rLength := #tmp_rLength;
            #udtGeo.rLeadIn := #i_rLeadIn;
            #udtGeo.rZ := #i_rZ;
            #udtGeo.rSafeZ := #i_rSafeZ;
            IF #i_rLiftZ <> 0.0 THEN
               #udtGeo.rLiftZ := #i_rLiftZ;
            ELSE
               #udtGeo.rLiftZ := #i_rSafeZ;
            END_IF;
            #udtGeo.rRotZEven := #tmp_rRotZEven;
            #udtGeo.rRotZOdd := #tmp_rRotZOdd;
            #udtGeo.udtPStart := #i_aoudtP[#P_START];
            #udtGeo.udtPHome := #i_aoudtP[#P_HOME];
            IF #i_xLiftBetween THEN
               #udtGeo.intMoves := 3 + (#tmp_intCount - 1) * 4 + 2;
            ELSE
               #udtGeo.intMoves := 3 + (#tmp_intCount - 1) * 2 + 2;
            END_IF;
            IF #tmp_intFirst = 1 THEN
               #udtGeo.intMoves := #udtGeo.intMoves + 1;
            END_IF;
            IF #udtGeo.xHome THEN
               #udtGeo.intMoves := #udtGeo.intMoves + 1;
            END_IF;

            // ---- the check before the first push, rule 9, without a list. every computed point of the job
            // lies inside the parallelogram of the four outer line ends: line 0 and line n-1, each from
            // -leadin to length + leadin along d. the limits are a box, so the four corners decide, at
            // every height the job uses (scan, safe, lift) and with both rotz values. then pose 2 and pose 1.
            // error 4 names the kind of the failing height (4 line, 2 above, 6 lift) and the line (0 or n-1)
            #tmp_udtP.rRotY := #udtGeo.rRotY;
            FOR #tmp_intC := 1 TO 4 DO
               IF #tmp_intC <= 2 THEN
                  #tmp_intK := 0;
               ELSE
                  #tmp_intK := #tmp_intCount - 1;
               END_IF;
               IF #tmp_intC = 1 OR #tmp_intC = 3 THEN
                  #tmp_rAlong := -#i_rLeadIn;
               ELSE
                  #tmp_rAlong := #tmp_rLength + #i_rLeadIn;
               END_IF;
               #tmp_rAX := #udtGeo.rA0X + INT_TO_REAL(#tmp_intK) * #udtGeo.rPitch * #udtGeo.rIdxX;
               #tmp_rAY := #udtGeo.rA0Y + INT_TO_REAL(#tmp_intK) * #udtGeo.rPitch * #udtGeo.rIdxY;
               #tmp_udtP.rX := #tmp_rAX + #tmp_rAlong * #udtGeo.rDirX;
               #tmp_udtP.rY := #tmp_rAY + #tmp_rAlong * #udtGeo.rDirY;
               FOR #tmp_intH := 1 TO 3 DO
                  IF #tmp_intH = 1 THEN
                     #tmp_udtP.rZ := #udtGeo.rZ;
                     #tmp_intKind := #ID_LINE;
                  ELSIF #tmp_intH = 2 THEN
                     #tmp_udtP.rZ := #udtGeo.rSafeZ;
                     #tmp_intKind := #ID_ABOVE;
                  ELSE
                     #tmp_udtP.rZ := #udtGeo.rLiftZ;
                     #tmp_intKind := #ID_LIFT;
                  END_IF;
                  IF #tmp_intH <> 3 OR #udtGeo.xLift THEN
                     FOR #tmp_intRot := 1 TO 2 DO
                        IF #tmp_intRot = 1 THEN
                           #tmp_udtP.rRotZ := #udtGeo.rRotZEven;
                        ELSE
                           #tmp_udtP.rRotZ := #udtGeo.rRotZOdd;
                        END_IF;
                        #tmp_intPoseErr := "FC_PoseCheck"(i_udtPose := #tmp_udtP);
                        IF #tmp_intPoseErr <> 0 AND #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
                           #tmp_intErr := 4;    // a point of the job is outside the limits
                           #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := #tmp_intKind;
                           #o_intLineActive := #tmp_intK;
                        END_IF;
                     END_FOR;
                  END_IF;
               END_FOR;
            END_FOR;
            IF #tmp_intErr = 0 AND #tmp_intFirst = 1 THEN
               IF "FC_PoseCheck"(i_udtPose := #udtGeo.udtPStart) <> 0 THEN
                  #tmp_intErr := 4;
                  #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := #ID_START;
                  #o_intLineActive := 0;
               END_IF;
            ELSIF #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
               IF "FC_PoseCheck"(i_udtPose := #udtGeo.udtPStart) <> 0 THEN
                  #tmp_intErr := 4;
                  #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := #ID_START2;
                  #o_intLineActive := 0;
               END_IF;
            END_IF;
            IF #tmp_intErr = 0 AND #udtGeo.xHome THEN
               IF "FC_PoseCheck"(i_udtPose := #udtGeo.udtPHome) <> 0 THEN
                  #tmp_intErr := 4;
                  #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := #ID_HOME;
                  #o_intLineActive := 0;
               END_IF;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;

         IF #tmp_intErr <> 0 THEN
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intErrId := #tmp_intErr;
            #intStep := 90;
         ELSE
            #o_udtOut.xClear := TRUE;           // whatever was left in the queue goes
            #intPushIdx := 1;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intMovesTotal := #udtGeo.intMoves;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intMovesDone := 0;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := 0;
            #o_intLineActive := 0;
            #o_intLineCount := #udtGeo.intCount;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.xRunning := TRUE;
            #intStep := 20;
         END_IF;

      20: // push while the queue has room, one entry per cycle. the engine already runs the first ones
         IF #i_intQueueCount < #QUEUE_KEEP THEN
            "FC_LineMove"(i_udtGeo := #udtGeo,
                          i_intIdx := #intPushIdx,
                          o_intKind => #tmp_intKind,
                          o_intK => #tmp_intK,
                          o_udtPose => #tmp_udtP);
            IF #tmp_intKind = #ID_DOWN0 OR #tmp_intKind = #ID_LINE OR #tmp_intKind = #ID_DOWN THEN
               #o_udtOut.udtPush.intBlock := #BLOCK_LIN_SLOW;
            ELSE
               #o_udtOut.udtPush.intBlock := #BLOCK_LIN;
            END_IF;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.udtPose := #tmp_udtP;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.udtPose2 := #tmp_udtP;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.rBlend := 0.0;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.aorPar[1] := 0.0;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.aorPar[2] := 0.0;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.aorPar[3] := 0.0;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.intOverride := #i_intOverride;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.xStopOnSensor := FALSE;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.intId := #tmp_intKind;
            #o_udtOut.udtPush.intPathLen := 0;    // a single move, always
            #o_udtOut.xPushReq := TRUE;
            #intPushIdx := #intPushIdx + 1;
            IF #intPushIdx > #udtGeo.intMoves THEN
               #intStep := 30;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;

      30: // run out. everything is pushed, the engine eats the rest
         IF #i_intQueueCount = 0 AND NOT #i_udtMoveState.xBusy AND NOT #i_udtMoveState.xDone THEN
            #o_udtOut.udtState.xRunning := FALSE;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.xDone := TRUE;
            #intStep := 0;
         END_IF;

      90: // error. stays until abort or the next start
         #o_udtOut.udtState.xRunning := FALSE;
         #o_udtOut.udtState.xError := TRUE;
         IF #tmp_xAbortEdge THEN
            #o_udtOut.udtState.xError := FALSE;
            #o_udtOut.udtState.intErrId := 0;
            #intStep := 0;
         END_IF;
   END_CASE;

   // ---- counting, steps 20 and 30. the moves run in the order of the list, so the active move is
   // the one after the finished ones. the kind comes from the engine's id, the line from fc_linemove
   IF #intStep = 20 OR #intStep = 30 THEN
      IF #i_udtMoveState.xDone THEN
         #o_udtOut.udtState.intMovesDone := #o_udtOut.udtState.intMovesDone + 1;
      END_IF;
      IF #i_udtMoveState.xBusy THEN
         #o_udtOut.udtState.intMoveActive := #i_udtMoveState.intIdActive;
         #tmp_intActive := #o_udtOut.udtState.intMovesDone + 1;
         IF #tmp_intActive >= 1 AND #tmp_intActive <= #udtGeo.intMoves THEN
            "FC_LineMove"(i_udtGeo := #udtGeo,
                          i_intIdx := #tmp_intActive,
                          o_intKind => #tmp_intKind,
                          o_intK => #tmp_intK,
                          o_udtPose => #tmp_udtP);
            #o_intLineActive := #tmp_intK;
         END_IF;
      END_IF;
   END_IF;

   // ---- the window bit: a line move runs and the actual x y lie inside the patch of that line.
   // the patch is the segment a_k .. a_k + length * d, the same for both directions. the actual pose is the
   // setpoint pose of the bus (pi 7 .. 11), late by one bus cycle; the lead-in covers that (SCAN_TYPES.md 3.2)
   #o_xScanWindow := FALSE;
   IF (#intStep = 20 OR #intStep = 30) AND #i_udtMoveState.xBusy AND #i_xActualValid
      AND #i_udtMoveState.intIdActive = #ID_LINE
      AND #o_intLineActive >= 0 AND #o_intLineActive < #udtGeo.intCount THEN
      #tmp_rAX := #udtGeo.rA0X + INT_TO_REAL(#o_intLineActive) * #udtGeo.rPitch * #udtGeo.rIdxX;
      #tmp_rAY := #udtGeo.rA0Y + INT_TO_REAL(#o_intLineActive) * #udtGeo.rPitch * #udtGeo.rIdxY;
      #tmp_rP := (#i_udtActual.rX - #tmp_rAX) * #udtGeo.rDirX
               + (#i_udtActual.rY - #tmp_rAY) * #udtGeo.rDirY;
      #o_xScanWindow := #tmp_rP >= 0.0 AND #tmp_rP <= #udtGeo.rLength;
   END_IF;

   #o_udtOut.udtState.intStep := #intStep;

   // job error numbers (the numbers of the cube and the drum job, plus 9)
   //  1 start (pose 2), the line start (pose 9), or corner 2 (pose 10, area mode) not taught
   //  2 safe z not set                                           4 a point of the job is outside the limits: intMoveActive = the kind, o_intLineActive = the line
   //  3 engine busy or in error at start                         5 length 0, pitch 0, lines outside 1 .. 5000, lead-in negative;
   //  6 scan from here not possible: not referenced or comm not ok    area mode: corner 2 gives no length, or more than 5000 lines
   //  9 the scan height is not above the face (rFaceZ set and rZ >= rFaceZ; smaller z is up)
   // 10 the engine went into error, see intEngineErr
   // the engine needs "DB_RobotMove".Cfg.intBlocksInPrg20 >= 2; 4 is in since the drum. nothing else on the robot
END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
